<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n55224" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατασπουδ-άζομαι</span></b>  (with
		aor.and pf.
		
			Pass.
		), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be earnest,
				serious</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				2.173
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐδαμῶς κατεσπουδασμένος
			ἀνήρ</span> ib. <i><span class="en">
				174
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κατεσπουδασμέναι δεήσεις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					11.61
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				4.67
			</span></i>:—later in 
				Act.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐὰν αὐτός τις . . φαίνηται -εσπουδακώς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Phld.
					<u>Mort.</u>
					31
				</span></i>
			: also c. dat., <i>take a serious interest in</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βλαβεροῖς κ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Mus.</u>
					p.56
				</span></i>
			 K.: abs., <i><span class="en">
				Apollon.
				<u>Lex.</u>
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπείγετον</span>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> as 
				Pass.
			, <i>to be troubled</i>, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Jb.</u>
				23.15
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Aq.
				<u>2 Ki.</u>
				4.1
			</span></i>, al. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>to be oppressed</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑπὸ
			μειζόνων</span> Vett. Val.<i><span class="en">
				254.16
			</span></i>.</div>
